## 15. Independent Scope V1 review request

Please perform an independent **design-only review** of:

`SVF-PRE-C4-AUTHORITY-GAP-SCOPE-V1`

The parent design, `SVF-PRE-C4-AUTHORITY-GAP-V2`, has already received:

`DESIGN_ACCEPTED_FOR_SEPARATE_AUTHORIZATION_CONSIDERATION`

Do not reopen previously accepted V2 design criteria unless the new scope creates a concrete contradiction or regression.

Please assess:

1. Whether the 15-document whitelist is appropriately bounded, exact and source-identifiable.
2. Whether all supplied SHA-256 bindings are explicitly provisional until independently checked.
3. Whether the GAP-01 through GAP-06 source mappings are substantively appropriate for documentary authority discovery.
4. Whether any mandatory governance authority source has been unjustifiably omitted from the proposed scope, considering the stated inspection purpose.
5. Whether D0270 and D0278 namespace identities remain independently distinguishable.
6. Whether the scope can produce defensible incomplete or negative bounded-discovery findings without inferring global rule nonexistence.
7. Whether integrity, activation, publication and scientific validity remain distinct.
8. Whether protected scientific artifacts, one-shot executions and Git mutation are excluded.
9. Whether source failure, missing evidence and incomplete coverage cause a fail-closed hold.
10. Whether scope design, independent review, freeze, effective inspection authorization and execution remain separate governance transactions.

Return `PASS`, `FAIL` or `NOT_VERIFIED` for each criterion, citing exact design sections.

Identify every mandatory correction explicitly.

Provide exactly one final recommendation:

- `DESIGN_ACCEPTED_FOR_SEPARATE_AUTHORIZATION_CONSIDERATION`
- `REVISION_REQUIRED`
- `INSUFFICIENT_GOVERNANCE_EVIDENCE`

Do not inspect the repository, open protected evidence, execute commands, adjudicate candidates, freeze the scope, grant inspection authorization or modify any existing scientific artifact during this review.

**Maintain `MAINTAIN_HOLD` until separately governed authorization and subsequent independently verified results establish otherwise.**
